00:21:55,150 --> 00:21:58,670
You can say, "Hey, our team's going to really follow an object-oriented pattern.

203
00:21:58,670 --> 00:22:07,550
Yes, we know it's not fully under the hood OOP, but we're able to pretty much at this point emulate many of the features, particularly now that there's private data in the last couple of years.

